    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "63b49de8_8298633a",
        "filename": "include/system.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 449,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-15T01:00:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "do we really need this - should\u0027t this be necessary only during CCD sesssions were sleep is disabled anyways.\n\nYes, conceivably one could be trying this from the console, but it is easier to plug in SuzyQ than to have a provision for this in the code.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 449,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 449,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "251480b44959b2af63b652bc5682f2336cee2142",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5dbabb72_8c0e6e1c",
        "filename": "include/system.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 449,
      "author": {
        "id": 1136059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-15T01:09:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As mentioned in the doc right now people can remove write protect without using suzyq. Not preventing deep sleep will make this a lot harder. Someone already needs to guess when to tap the power button. If for some reason the process fails because the device randomly enters deep sleep, it\u0027s going to get pretty frustrating.",
      "parentUuid": "63b49de8_8298633a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 449,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 449,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "251480b44959b2af63b652bc5682f2336cee2142",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "53d4ca0b_e240e61e",
        "filename": "include/system.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 449,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-15T01:20:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this should be addressed by delaying sleep after power for a few minutes. Having this whole logic of using yet another bit in the mask and having the code to call enable/disable sleep in multiple places is not worth it IMO.\n\nThe power on sleep delay increase may be conditional on this property (delayed WP).",
      "parentUuid": "5dbabb72_8c0e6e1c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 449,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 449,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "251480b44959b2af63b652bc5682f2336cee2142",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b57ab4d3_0bd56209",
        "filename": "include/system.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 449,
      "author": {
        "id": 1136059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-15T01:28:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "the cr50 system timer continues counting in deep sleep. When it expires, cr50 wakes up briefly, resets it then enters deep sleep. This happens every about once every hour and a half.\n\ndeep sleep power is like 1.5mw regular sleep is 7mw and active power is 50mw.\n\nIf there is a device that isn\u0027t owned but has the battery or wp screw removed, then that device will start this process every time it resumes from deep sleep. That means once every hour and a half cr50 will consume 50mW for 7 minutes when the device is suspended/off.\n\nI think this is a lot of power. Will we just say if you remove the battery or write protect screw, then your power consumption doesn\u0027t matter?",
      "parentUuid": "53d4ca0b_e240e61e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 449,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 449,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "251480b44959b2af63b652bc5682f2336cee2142",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "031f4dbb_6450a33f",
        "filename": "include/system.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 449,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-15T17:27:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So is the proposal is to use delay_sleep_by() at the start of the process?  Setting the delay time to ((BATT_REMOVE_PHYSICAL_PRESENCE_TIME + BUTTON_PRESS_TIMEOUT)/MSEC) - or 7 minutes.",
      "parentUuid": "b57ab4d3_0bd56209",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 449,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 449,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "251480b44959b2af63b652bc5682f2336cee2142",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0f74386f_3d47cc71",
        "filename": "include/system.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 449,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-15T17:35:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "the proposal is to delay entering sleep post reset if battery is disconnected.\n\nJust add a call to delay_sleep_by(interval); to board startup code, to be invoked if running with battery disconnected (and maybe only on devices where the appropriate property is set by strapping resistors)",
      "parentUuid": "031f4dbb_6450a33f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 449,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 449,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "251480b44959b2af63b652bc5682f2336cee2142",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5a818471_f4b3336d",
        "filename": "include/system.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 470,
      "author": {
        "id": 1136059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-15T00:20:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not sure what this does, but it almost certainly does not only disable deep sleep. It looks like idle.c uses this to determine if cr50 can enter any form of sleep. It uses idle_action to determine if it should enter regular sleep or deep sleep.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 470,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 470,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "251480b44959b2af63b652bc5682f2336cee2142",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
